def GlobalDocumentation {
  code Intro =[{..
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  NOTE: This file is automatically generated by running llvm-tblgen
  -gen-kit-module-attr-doc. Do not edit this file by hand!!
  -------------------------------------------------------------------

===============================
LLVM Module Attribute Reference
===============================
.. contents::
  :local:

.. |br| raw:: html

  <br/>

These are Kitsune-specific "attributes" that may be added to LLVM modules. More
general information about creating and using Kitsune's LLVM IR attributes can be
found :doc:`here <LLVMIRAttributes>`.

These appear as named metadata nodes in the module. Each attribute may take some
number of values. For a given attribute, the number of values and their types
are fixed. These values may be integers, strings or enums.

In the example below, two attributes are added to the module,
:ref:`kit.module.device.module.flags <module-attr-device-module-flags>`, and
:ref:`kit.module.pre.lower.annotate.pass <module-attr-pre-lower-annotate-pass>`.
The first of these has a number of values, while the other has no values.

.. code :: kitll

  ; ModuleID = 'aberystwyth'
  target triple = "riscv64-pc-freebsd"

  !kit.module.device.metadata.flags = !{!0, !1}
  !kit.module.pre.lower.annotate.pass = !{}

  !0 = !{i32 2}
  !1 = !{!"loughborough"}

Every attribute has an entry in the ``ModuleAttrKind`` enum.
}];
}

include "kitsune/Core/ModuleAttrs.td"
